# Google Analytics 4

Use **GA4 only** with Measurement ID **`G-HT76VNZHG5`**. Never use Universal Analytics or other measurement IDs.

## Initialization

- GA4 is initialized in `src/main.tsx` via `initGoogleAnalytics()` from `src/lib/analytics.ts`.
- Analytics runs **only in production** (`import.meta.env.PROD`) and **only after full cookie consent**.
- Do not add gtag.js snippets to `index.html`; loading is consent-gated in `analytics.ts`.

## Page views

- SPA route changes are tracked in `App.tsx` via `trackPageView()` (see `GoogleAnalyticsPageViews`).
- Initial `gtag("config")` uses `send_page_view: false` to avoid duplicate first page views.
- Do not call `gtag("config", …)` directly for navigation; use `trackPageView()`.

## Custom events

Import helpers from `src/lib/analytics.ts`:

```typescript
import { trackEvent } from "../lib/analytics.ts"

trackEvent("button_click", { button_name: "post_job" })
```

Use `trackEvent()` for all custom events. Do not call `window.gtag` directly.

## CSP

When adding new analytics domains, update `security/csp.mjs` and `public/_headers` to allow:
- `https://www.googletagmanager.com` (script-src)
- `https://www.google-analytics.com`, `https://analytics.google.com`, `https://*.google-analytics.com` (connect-src)
